### Test OIDC Client Credentials Flow for Initializer Token
### This file tests the OIDC token endpoint with the initializer credentials

### Variables - Update these based on your environment
@authDomain = http://auth.crystal-image.net
@clientId = f63672873ab7908f14f889c9a4d1b0747b8036257aa08c3568f5b1aa102f75d2
@clientSecret = T7uAqmC0utEiQO4ifCDvlnscjFTxaV8/XLPngmA7phCCif8mZy25MrTTu9OaDRPs
@host = www.crystal-image.net

### 1. Get Client Credentials Token (Initializer Token)
### This is what the InitializerTokenStrategy.refreshToken() calls
POST {{authDomain}}/oidc/token
Host: {{host}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}&scope=tenant:read

### 2. Alternative - Test without scope
POST {{authDomain}}/oidc/token
Host: {{host}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}

### 3. Test Token Introspection (if you have a token)
### Replace {access_token} with actual token from response above
# @name tokenResponse
POST {{authDomain}}/oidc/introspect
Host: {{host}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

token={access_token}&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}

### 4. Test Tenant API with Initializer Token
### First get the token from request #1, then use it here
### Replace {access_token} with actual token
GET http://api.crystal-image.net/tenant/settings?id=688602a2c856ff5ae49faecb
Host: {{host}}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
x-tenant-id: 688602a2c856ff5ae49faecb

### 5. Test if auth service is reachable
GET {{authDomain}}/health
Host: {{host}}
Accept: application/json

### 6. Test OIDC Discovery Endpoint (if available)
GET {{authDomain}}/.well-known/openid-configuration
Host: {{host}}
Accept: application/json

###
### DEBUGGING NOTES:
### 
### Common Issues:
### 1. Network Error: Check if auth.crystal-image.net is reachable
### 2. 401 Unauthorized: Check client_id and client_secret
### 3. 400 Bad Request: Check grant_type and request format
### 4. Connection Refused: Auth service might be down
###
### The InitializerTokenStrategy flow:
### 1. Checks Redis cache for existing token
### 2. If not found or expired, calls refreshToken()
### 3. refreshToken() gets credentials from env vars
### 4. Calls getClientCredentialsToken() which makes the POST to /oidc/token
### 5. Stores the token in Redis cache with expiry
###
### Environment Variables Required:
### - TENANT_API_CLIENT_ID
### - TENANT_API_CLIENT_SECRET
### - AUTH_DOMAIN (optional, defaults based on current domain)
###